    "title": {
     "en": "Paper strings"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Children cut paper strings of different colours to decorate the board. Which is the longest and which is the shortest?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "ruler",
     "zero",
     "tape",
     "measure"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Take a ruler and look at the marks. Each small mark is a centimetre.\nPut the zero mark at the start of the string and read the number at its end.\nMeasure each paper string. The one with the biggest number is the longest.\nMeasure the height of the window and find a string just as long.\nTo measure something longer than the ruler, use a tape or mark the end and move the ruler on.\nWrite measures with units, like 12 cm."
    }
